==English==

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|ydropsy}}, from {{der|en|fro|idropsie}}, {{m|fro|ydropisie}}, from {{der|en|la|hydropisis}}, from {{der|en|grc|ὕδρωψ|}}, from {{m|grc|ὕδωρ|t=water}}. {{doublet|en|hydropsy}}, {{m|en|hydrops}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|-|dropsies}}

# {{lb|en|pathology}} Swelling, [[edema]], often from chronic obstructive pulmonary disease ([[COPD]]).
#* '''1911''', ''Joseph Addison'', [[S:1911 Encyclopædia Britannica/Addison, Joseph|Encyclopædia Britannica]]:
#*: The disease under which Addison laboured appears to have been asthma. It became more violent after his retirement from office, and was now accompanied by '''dropsy'''.

